#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# beta_regularized

#% text
# `beta_regularized(z, a, b)` gives the regularized incomplete beta function `beta(z, a, b)/beta(a, b)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `beta_regularized(z, a, b)` is `I_z(a, b)` of DLMF 8.17.2; it rises from 0 at `z = 0` to 1 at `z = 1`, and it is the distribution function of the beta distribution.

#% item
# Integer parameters with exact `z` give exact values; machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% item
# `beta_regularized` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
beta_regularized(1/2, 2, 3)
#% output
#= beta_regularized(1/2, 2, 3)

#% cell
beta_regularized(0.3, 2.5, 4.0)
#% output
#= 0.3521975859067672

#% cell
beta_regularized(z, 1, 2)
#% output
#= beta_regularized(z, 1, 2)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The probability of at most 3 successes in 10 trials of chance 0.5, from the binomial-beta relation:

#% cell
1 - beta_regularized(0.5, 4, 7)
#% output
#= 0.171875

#% cell
n(sum(binomial(10, k), [k, 0, 3])/2^10)
#% output
#= 0.171875

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The symmetry `I_z(a, b) = 1 - I_(1 - z)(b, a)`:

#% cell
beta_regularized(0.2, 3.0, 5.0) + beta_regularized(0.8, 5.0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 1.0

#% text
# The inverse:

#% cell
inverse_beta_regularized(beta_regularized(0.4, 2.0, 3.0), 2.0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.4

